+### Accelerometer bias during stationary initialization
+
+For a stationary IMU, the mean measured specific force obeys
+
+\[
+\bar f_m^b=R(q_{wb})^Tg^w+b_a^b,\qquad g^w=[0,0,g]^T.
+\]
+
+When roll and pitch are initialized from the same acceleration mean, only the
+bias component parallel to body-frame gravity is observable. With
+\(n^b=\bar f_m^b/\lVert\bar f_m^b\rVert\), the initializer reports
+
+\[
+b_{a,\parallel}^b=(\lVert\bar f_m^b\rVert-g)n^b
+=\bar f_m^b-R(q_{wb})^Tg^w.
+\]
+
+Bias perpendicular to gravity is indistinguishable from roll/pitch error in a
+single stationary pose and is not initialized. The ROS component injects this
+observable component only when `stationary_initialization_estimate_accel_bias`
+is enabled; it is disabled by default for compatibility.
+
 ### Absolute orientation and course yaw
 
 For quaternion measurement \(q_z\), the innovation is the shortest-arc log map
